(1. Topic Introduction) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf
0 -14 Td
(MongoDB is the leading NoSQL document-oriented database system designed for agility, horizontal scalability, and developer) Tj
0 -12 Td
(productivity. It stores semi-structured data in BSON format, offering flexible schemas and powerful expressive query capabilities.) Tj
0 -12 Td
0 -7 Td
/F2 12 Tf
0 -16 Td
(2. Important Concepts) Tj
/F1 9.5 Tf
0 -14 Td
(- Document Data Model: JSON/BSON records containing polymorphic key-value pairs, nested subdocuments, and arrays.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(- Data Modeling Strategies: Embedding documents \(one-to-few\) versus referencing ObjectIds \(one-to-many/many-to-many\).) Tj
0 -12 Td
(- CRUD Operations: createIndex, find, insertOne, updateMany, and deleteOne commands with atomic update operators \($set, $push\).) Tj
0 -12 Td
(- Aggregation Framework: Pipeline stages including $match, $group, $lookup \(left joins\), $project, $sort, and $unwind.) Tj
0 -12 Td
(- Indexing & Sharding: Single field, compound, text, and TTL indexes; horizontal scaling via sharded cluster partitions.) Tj
0 -12 Td
0 -7 Td
